.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBFlowGrid\fR: items of equal size that flow into columns, after Mantine's \fBSimpleGrid\fR. Either a fixed number of columns (\fBcols\fR: one column is a list) or as many as fit, each at most \fBmax_width\fR wide. The items fill their cells, and \fBa row\fR shares one height\fB, that of its tallest item: every item is laid out again at that height, so\fR a card whose title wraps does not leave its neighbours short (CSS grid's \fBalign\-items:\fR stretch\fB, the rows of a subgrid). An item stretches if its own surface fits its content\fR (\fBLength::Shrink\fR), as a card does. Albums, playlists, apps, projects.
.PP
\fBrow_height\fR chooses: \fBShared\fR (default), \fBOwn\fR or \fBFixed\fR.
.PP
The layout is the grid of iced's \fBGrid\fR (same column rule), with that second pass. When cells should differ in width, use a \fBTableGrid\fR.
.PP
.nf
.RS
FlowGrid::new(albums.iter().map(album_card)).max_width(180.0)
FlowGrid::new(albums.iter().map(album_row)).cols(1)   // a list
.RE
.fi
